Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:22:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] vocab edges at a world that does not divide them:
 block-aligned split, declared as a span

token_embd / output are RAD_SHARD_ROW; at three ranks 248320 rows do not
divide, and share.cpp refuses a row shard without a declared span.
qwen4exp now declares [vocab_off, vocab_off + n_vocab) for both. The split
rule (rad_arch.h shard_extent/shard_begin, restated in core/engine.cpp)
keeps the even share whenever the world divides the vocabulary -- two and
four ranks are untouched -- and only otherwise rounds the per-rank count
up to a 128-row block, because a block-scaled fp8 head refuses a cut
inside a tile: at three the ranks take 82816, 82816, 82688.
---
